spans.s:
व॑ज्र m. n. thunderbolt (flash of lightning), esp.
conceived as the weapon of Indra;
 diamond (mostly n.);
 m. a form of
military array (±व्यूह), N. of sev. men, also = वज्रलेप. n. a
thunder-like i.e. very hard word.

वज्राय् वज्रा˚यते become a thunderbolt or diamond;
 pp.
˚यमान hard, adamantine.

वा॑ज m. swiftness, strength, courage;
 race, struggle,
contest & its prize, booty, gain, reward, treasure, good;
 offering -
meat;
 runner, horse;
 N. of one of the Ṛbhus, pl. the Ṛbhus together^1.
[1] Correction submitted by AnnaRybakovaT, Jim Funderburk. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/25.

वाजय् वाज॑यति & वाजय॑ति वाजय॑˚ते run for the
prize, race, hasten;
 combat, contest;
 spur on, incite.

वाजस॑नि a. gaining or granting good, booty, strength,
etc.;
 victorious.

वाजसनेय॑ m. patron. of Yājñavalkya;
 pl. N. of a
Vedic school.
